 \subsection*{IV 20.7: Application to hyperplane sections and multisections of specified type (cote 25, sites 27--30)}
-This section turns the preceding open subsets of the dual projective space into families of hyperplane sections and then into multisections. The discussion moves from rational points over an infinite field to sections near a chosen base point, and then to finite separable residue-field extensions and an étale change of base. The author redirects the flatness argument from the old references 4.7--4.8 to the revised number 5 on site 28. A canceled preliminary passage on that page gives way to the remords on site 29: the singular locus for a property P is allowed to have a specified dimension, and the resulting formulations 7.2--7.3 track its dimension after taking a hyperplane section. The margin adds another case to 4.3 through published EGA IV 12.2.1, with the final parenthesized reference still doubtful. The two expanded subscripts on site 29 visibly read $\xi,\xi(s)$, while the intervening G has only $\xi(s)$; the neighborhood is printed as a neighborhood of s ``dans E''. Those forms remain in the text. Proposition 7.4 and remarks 7.5 develop the construction of étale multisections, including the successive reduction of fiber dimension; the final marginal note proposes avoiding an ensemble whose faint adjective remains doubtful. The canceled discussion across sites 29--30 invokes EGA III 7 and Stein factorization for geometric connected components. Its replacement margin cites EGA IV 12.2.1, with the first Roman numeral unresolved and the second legibly(xi). The earlier canceled Remords on site 27 separates openness by the valuative criterion from the flatness conclusion using EGA IV 15.2.2; it records a proposed reorganization of 4.6--4.8, rather than a completed renumbering. Sources: \href{https://grothendieck.umontpellier.fr/web/viewer.html?file=../25.pdf\#page=28}{site 27}, \href{https://grothendieck.umontpellier.fr/web/viewer.html?file=../25.pdf\#page=29}{site 28}, \href{https://grothendieck.umontpellier.fr/web/viewer.html?file=../25.pdf\#page=30}{site 29}, and \href{https://grothendieck.umontpellier.fr/web/viewer.html?file=../25.pdf\#page=31}{site 30}.
